  "claim": "The bank famously opposed by Brendan Bracken for co-operation with Adolf Hitler was originally established in 1694.",
  "evidencia": "Page: Brendan Bracken. Sentence: Brendan Bracken, 1st Viscount Bracken, PC (15 February 1901 – 8 August 1958), was an Irish born businessman and a minister in the British Conservative cabinet.\nPage: Brendan Bracken. Sentence: He is best remembered for opposing the Bank of England's co-operation with Adolf Hitler, and for subsequently supporting Winston Churchill's prosecution of World War II against Hitler.\nPage: Bank of England. Sentence: The Bank of England, formally the Governor and Company of the Bank of England, is the central bank of the United Kingdom and the model on which most modern central banks have been based.\nPage: Bank of England. Sentence: Established in 1694, it is the second oldest central bank in operation today, after the Sveriges Riksbank.",
  "evidence_text": "Page: Brendan Bracken. Sentence: Brendan Bracken, 1st Viscount Bracken, PC (15 February 1901 – 8 August 1958), was an Irish born businessman and a minister in the British Conservative cabinet.\nPage: Brendan Bracken. Sentence: He is best remembered for opposing the Bank of England's co-operation with Adolf Hitler, and for subsequently supporting Winston Churchill's prosecution of World War II against Hitler.\nPage: Bank of England. Sentence: The Bank of England, formally the Governor and Company of the Bank of England, is the central bank of the United Kingdom and the model on which most modern central banks have been based.\nPage: Bank of England. Sentence: Established in 1694, it is the second oldest central bank in operation today, after the Sveriges Riksbank.",
