        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "0ca95e6b-0278-5232-8d34-dc37bb0a7baa",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Brendan Bracken, Winston Churchill, Adolf Hitler\n- Organizations: Bank of England\n- Roles: British Conservative cabinet minister, businessman, central bank\n- Places: United Kingdom, Ireland\n- Topics: World War II, central banking\n\nFacts:\n- The Bank of England was established in 1694.\n- The Bank of England is formally called the Governor and Company of the Bank of England.\n- The Bank of England is the central bank of the United Kingdom and served as the model for most modern central banks.\n- The Bank of England is the second oldest central bank still operating, after the Sveriges Riksbank.\n- Brendan Bracken was born in Ireland on 15 February 1901.\n- Brendan Bracken was a businessman and a minister in the British Conservative cabinet.\n- Brendan Bracken is remembered for opposing the Bank of England's co-operation with Adolf Hitler.\n- Brendan Bracken later supported Winston Churchill's prosecution of World War II against Adolf Hitler.\n- Brendan Bracken died on 8 August 1958.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
